            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/why-primary-polls-appear-to-be-so-inaccurate-this-year</link>
            <description><![CDATA[Results in some high-profile races this primary season have differed greatly from public opinion polls. In the Michigan Senate Democratic primary, progressive Abdul El-Sayed had double-digit leads in polling but won over Haley Stevens by just one point. Lisa Desjardins and Courtney Kennedy of Ipsos discussed the recent results that were at odds with polling.]]></description>
